Test Case ID	Module	Test Scenario	Preconditions	Test Steps	Test Data	Expected Result	Actual Result	Status
TC_AUTH_REG_001	Authentication - Registration	Verify that a user can register successfully with valid details	1. Backend is running.2. Test DB is connected.3. Email is not already registered.	1. Send POST /api/auth/register.2. Provide valid registration details.3. Verify response status.4. Verify token and user details.5. Verify user is stored in DB.6. Verify password is hashed.	Name: New Test UserEmail: newuser@example.comPassword: Test@123Role: Receptionist	API returns 201 Created.Token is returned.User details are returned without password.User is created in MongoDB.Password is stored as a hash.	API returned 201.Token and user details were returned.Password was not exposed.User was created in the test DB with a hashed password.	Pass
TC_AUTH_REG_002	Authentication - Registration	Verify that registration is rejected when the email already exists	1. Backend is running.2. Test DB is connected.3. A user with the test email already exists.	1. Create an existing user in the test DB.2. Send POST /api/auth/register with the same email.3. Verify response status.4. Verify error message.5. Verify no token/user is returned.	Name: Another UserEmail: existing@example.comPassword: Another@123Role: Receptionist	API returns 400 Bad Request.Response message is User already exists.No token or user object is returned.Duplicate user is not created.	API returned 400 with User already exists.No token or user object was returned.	Pass
